  "term": "mental health program",
  "definition": "A mental health program is an organized service model that provides mental health support, such as case management, counseling, psychiatric consultation, and short-term follow-up care. In this source, it is described as a flexible, hub-based program that helps primary care doctors connect patients with mental health, hospital, and community resources.",
